MODIFIED VERSION OF CHAPIDIF
Allow to use chapidif without GUI, compute and plot with more freedom.
TO DO:
  - Add Born-Ochkur exchange factor
  - Allow to modify the energy integration limit
  - Add step function for Mermin


The binary distributions are self-contained and do not require python or any additional packages. Just unzip the file for your platform, and run the file named chapidif.

installation from source:
It requires a C compiler (GCC was used) and the folllowing (widely-used) python packages:
matplotlib, pyqt6, numpy, nanobind.

copy the files with  with subfolders to a place of your choice.
execute the script "configure_and_build" in either the LinuxLib or WindowsLib subdirectory.
This creates the library.  After that chapidif.py can be run like any python program. 

if problems, do not hesitate to ask:  maarten.vos@anu.edu.au
